WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
Lakeview isn't the same place [after Katrina] because . . . You know, sometimes people tell you, "My house burned down.

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.160
I know how you feel having lost everything."

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.940
When I . . . When we lost everything in Lakeview,

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:16.500
we also lost our neighbors, we lost our church, we lost our grocery store, our drugstore.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.860
Some of that has come back.

6
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.380
But the bagger that bagged our groceries, we don't know what happened to him.

7
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.880
That lady that worked at the cleaners, we don't know what happened to her.

8
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.480
It certainly is coming back, but it's not the same place.

9
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:38.900
So when somebody says they know how it feels, I don't know that anybody really knows how that feels.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:51.180
It was . . . It was a day that changed our lives forever.

11
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:58.360
My mother . . . You know I always put this as an addendum, that my mother was eighty-five when Katrina hit.

12
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.220
I think people around the country think that we flooded all the time.

13
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:08.700
My mother had never been involved in a flood, had never lost anything in a flood.

14
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.700
Betsy came up to our steps, but never came into our house.

15
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.340
So it was a new thing for all of us.

16
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.520
My mother's sister had flooded for Betsy because she was in St. Bernard [Parish].

17
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.120
But, you know, we didn't flood.

18
00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:25.920
We didn't know what it was like to lose our wedding pictures and lose everything.
